{
  "VOID_NOT_A_SCORED_REPLAY_RUN": {
    "declared_at_utc": "2026-11-06T20:33:24Z",
    "not_done_because_of_this": "no decision.md for this run, no G3 position, no H3 verdict, nothing sealed from it.",
    "status": "VOID for H3. This is not a measurement of replay. Do not score it, quote it, or seal it as STEP 5.",
    "what_STEP_5_needs_to_be_run_for_real": "launch the replay arm as a SUBPROCESS, the way the sealed replay_tier120_armA.json was produced, so the __main__ guard parses --replay; then require the artifact to carry a replay report at every depth and refuse the run if it does not. The same-process constraint belongs to the floor pair, which is already sealed, not to the treated and untreated runs.",
    "what_is_still_valid_here": {
      "A10_resource_ledger": "measured and available on both runs -- sampler active, 2,392 samples, VRAM asserted zero. This is the first A10 ledger on a tier-120 run in this program, and it stands as an instrument measurement, not as a score.",
      "mouth_stage_attribution_limitation": "every failing row classified as recall_untraced because the bench does not record a `reason` per row (rows carry reason: \"\"), and the registered classifier returns recall_untraced for an empty reason. So the five-stage denominator cannot discriminate on bench rows: that is a property of the instrument, not a finding about the organism. H1's instrument is heldout_eval over the held-out script set, which has no --state-root and cannot be pointed at a bench workdir.",
      "preflight": "the configuration, phase basis and gain were quoted from the ledger before the first scored minute and resolved to single lines, including the two spans needed because a one-line needle for the ceiling and the margin matched three and two lines respectively",
      "same_process_proof": {
        "all_agree": true,
        "samples": [
          14404,
          14404,
          14404,
          14404
        ],
        "statement": "four pid samples taken around both runs. If they do not agree the pair cannot prove same-process and this run does not score."
      },
      "wall_clock": {
        "control_run_seconds": 443.36,
        "replay_labelled_run_seconds": 493.89
      }
    },
    "what_the_argv_claims": [
      "--arms",
      "learn",
      "--curriculum",
      "experiments/MP-E8/curriculum_tier120.json",
      "--out",
      "experiments/MP-E10/results/step5_tier120_replay_armA.json",
      "--workdir",
      "_tmp/wd_step5_replay",
      "--replay"
    ],
    "what_the_artifact_actually_contains": {
      "reading": "the house records no replay at any depth, so no replay executed. The argv still names --replay, which is why the file is self-contradictory and why this block exists.",
      "replay_report_present_in_any_run": false,
      "runs_in_the_replay_house": 3
    },
    "what_the_two_runs_really_were": "two unreplayed tier-120 runs in one process -- a third fresh-vs-fresh pair, not a treatment comparison. Its 6 rows of 3,744 exactly equals the pair-5 floor of 6 rows, which is a consistency check on the floor and nothing more. It says nothing about replay, in either direction.",
    "why": "the driver invoked bench.main() in-process. The bench sets REPLAY_REQUESTED from REPLAY_REQUESTED_AT_MAIN, and that is assigned only inside the `if __name__ == \"__main__\":` guard (tools/electric_learn_bench.py:423-426), which does not run for an importing process. So REPLAY_REQUESTED stayed False, the replay branch at :751 was skipped without error, and the run produced an unreplayed house under a filename that says replay."
  },
